.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_KDF-PKCS12KDF 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_KDF-PKCS12KDF
.Nd The PKCS#12 EVP_KDF implementation
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Support for computing the
.Sy PKCS#12
password-based KDF through the
.Sy EVP_KDF
API.
.Pp
The EVP_KDF-PKCS12KDF algorithm implements the PKCS#12 password-based
key derivation function, as described in appendix B of RFC 7292 (PKCS
#12: Personal Information Exchange Syntax); it derives a key from a
password using a salt, iteration count and the intended usage.
.Ss Identity
"PKCS12KDF" is the name for this implementation; it can be used with the
.Xr EVP_KDF_fetch 3
function.
.Ss Supported parameters
The supported parameters are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqpass" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_PASSWORD Ns ) <octet string>
.It \(dqsalt" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SALT Ns ) <octet string>
.It \(dqiter" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_ITER Ns ) <unsigned integer>
.It \(dqproperties" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_PROPERTIES Ns ) <UTF8 string>
.It \(dqdigest" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_DIGEST Ns ) <UTF8 string>
These parameters work as described in
.Xr EVP_KDF 3 .
.It \(dqid" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_PKCS12_ID Ns ) <integer>
This parameter is used to specify the intended usage of the output bits,
as per RFC 7292 section B.3.
.El
.Sh NOTES
This algorithm is not available in the FIPS provider as it is not FIPS
approvable.
.Pp
A typical application of this algorithm is to derive keying material for
an encryption algorithm from a password in the "pass", a salt in "salt",
and an iteration count.
.Pp
Increasing the "iter" parameter slows down the algorithm which makes it
harder for an attacker to perform a brute force attack using a large
number of candidate passwords.
.Pp
No assumption is made regarding the given password; it is simply treated
as a byte sequence.
.Sh CONFORMING TO
RFC7292
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_KDF 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF_CTX_new 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF_CTX_free 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF_CTX_set_params 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF_derive 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF 3 ,
.Xr OSSL_PROVIDER-FIPS 7
